  "discipline": "Every authored fixture is digest-pinned per file. Every authored fixture states expected outcome ACCEPT or exactly one refusal family/subcode. Windows-only path classes stay absent (D-002). Ceremony-validity (wrong key, expired metadata, revoked namespace, threshold failure) remains DR-112 and is not in this corpus. ENVELOPE_MISMATCH remains conditional on ID-DEP-1 and ID-DEP-5.",
  "honestyRepairsThisRevision": [
    "TC-NAME.alias-cycle is now a mutual command-alias cycle (cmd-a <-> cmd-b), not alias-equals-name",
    "TC-SIG.digest-mismatch is a single-byte flip of TC-ACCEPT.minimal stored bytes; recorded digest is the unflipped source",
    "TC-ACCEPT.maximal and TC-ACCEPT.approved-exception now have distinct stableIds so they can coexist with minimal",
    "TC-ACCEPT.index-all-accept carries minimal, multiversion-v2, maximal, and approved-exception",
    "TC-ACCEPT.lock-multi-component resolves a two-component closure (maximal depends on minimal)"
  ],
